YW5rYXRyYXZlbHBhZ2VzLmNvbS9wbGFjZXMtdG8tdmlzaXQtaW4tbmVnb21iby1zcmktbGFua2Ev&amp;ntb=1" h="ID=SERP,5519.1">The stunning beaches and water sports make Negombo must and explore list of places to visit in Negombo in Sri Lanka</a></div></div></div></li></ul></div><div class="b_wpt_bl colSpan5 rowSpan2 b_wpt_bl_h b_wpt_bl_back" data-appns="SERP" data-k="5182"><a data-priority="2" class="b_lcs_quilting_card" target="_blank" href="https://www.bing.com/ck/a?!&amp;&amp;p=aa6ffd4ab4ad42511914a0efab37bb04e33a659824b609a32cb07ebf7f38d311JmltdHM9MTc3NTg2NTYwMA&amp;ptn=3&amp;ver=2&amp;hsh=4&amp;fclid=2ef4c5e4-2b7f-6993-331e-d0e82a3a6873&amp;psq=negombo+trevl+pages&amp;u=a1aHR0cHM6Ly9zcmlsYW5rYXRyYXZlbHBhZ2VzLmNvbS9wbGFjZXMtdG8tdmlzaXQtaW4tbmVnb21iby1zcmktbGFua2Ev&amp;ntb=1" h="ID=SERP,5523.1"><div class="b_lcs_title">11 Places to Visit in <strong>Negombo</strong> – Sri Lanka</div><div class="b_lcs_steps"><div class="b_lcs_step">1. Negombo Beach. Negombo’s beach fronts are the primary motive for travellers visiting this city. The golden beaches and stunning hideaways on the seaside complete your holiday in this city.</div><div class="b_lcs_step">2. Hamilton Canal. Hamilton Canal, Negombo, titled after a British Government representative, and canal about 10 km long, joining the lagoon with the river entrance of the Maha Oya.</div><div class="b_lcs_step">3. Negombo Lagoon. Negombo Dutch Fort is located in the City of Negombo. Initially a Portuguese formulation, it was restored by the Dutch after they caught that city.</div><div class="b_lcs_step">4. Negombo Dutch Fort. Negombo Dutch Fort is located in the City of Negombo. Initially a Portuguese formulation, it was restored by the Dutch after they caught that city.</div><div class="b_lcs_step">5. Anugurukaramulla Temple. St. Mary’s Church, located on Grand Street in the heart of Negombo, a rose-coloured Roman Catholic cathedral, is one of the most magnificent churches in Sri Lanka.</div></div></a></div></div><div class="slide wptSld 